1. Assign a RESP-ID and describe it (solution-neutral).
2. Add responsibility_constraints (RC-X-Y) from constraint requirements.
3. Derive process model parts (PM-X-Y) — what information the controller needs.
4. Derive control actions (CA-X-Y) — what outputs the controller produces, with targets.
5. Derive feedback channels (FB-X-Y) — what updates each PM part, with sources.

Identify controlled processes (CP-*) for entities that are not responsibilities but are referenced by feedback sources or control action targets.
